Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: or

asr-000165
00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: motu proprio inquiry

asr-000166
00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:47.380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: into the conduct of oil companies

asr-000167
00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.600
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: during that period?

asr-000168
00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.700
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: PCC is conducting

asr-000169
00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.800
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: a fuel study

asr-000170
00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:56.740
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: which aims to assess

asr-000171
00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:59.000
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: asymmetry in price adjustments.

asr-000172
00:14:59.740 --> 00:15:00.300
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Example,

asr-000173
00:15:00.785 --> 00:15:21.680
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: When stations price increase rapidly with international prices but adjust slowly when this cost decrease, it also aims to look at price dispersion within a city and determine whether particular stations or brands show delayed rollback or remain persistently above local market prices.

asr-000174
00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:28.640
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The study is ongoing pending data requests with fuel players and government agencies.

asr-000175
00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:40.340
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: PCC has started gathering and analyzing industry data to determine whether firm behavior during this time reflect a competitive environment or not.

asr-000176
00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:47.660
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Specifically looking at how firms adjust prices with and without the supply shocks.

asr-000177
00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:57.060
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: PCC issued requests for information to key players in the industry, some of which have complied with the request.

asr-000178
00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:59.980
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: At present, the PCC is analyzing the industry data.

asr-000179
00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:08.360
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC is analyzing the data to determine whether the behavior of the key players indicate possible anti-competitive conduct.

asr-000180
00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:15.100
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC has received request data from the DOA today, September 18, 2026.

asr-000181
00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.360
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000182
00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:29.980
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Good Sponsor, a few days ago, I have raised urgent concerns related to privacy risks in digital platforms.

asr-000183
00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:51.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Incidentally, I came across the information that PCC's market study on social media and search platform found that the Philippines' digital platform market is highly concentrated and identified the accumulation of user data as a potential source of market power.

asr-000184
00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:58.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It specifically discussed Facebook and Google and observed that data advantages,

asr-000185
00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:05.760
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: network effects, and economies of scale may reinforce barriers to entry.

asr-000186
00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:12.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: What does the PCC intend to do with these findings beyond publishing the market study?

asr-000187
00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:22.840
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC has recommended incorporating data privacy considerations more explicitly into competition assessments.

asr-000188
00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:27.840
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Studying data, portability, and interoperability.

asr-000189
00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:39.600
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Strengthening coordination with privacy regulators and considering legislative measures to update the competition framework for data-driven markets.

asr-000190
00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:44.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000191
00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:54.420
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: In 2024, the PCC received substantial resources for the capacity building to foster competition projects,

asr-000192
00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.700
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: but only 34% of the continuing...

asr-000193
00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.540
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: appropriation for the foreign-assisted project was obligated.

asr-000194
00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:03.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is that correct?

asr-000195
00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:07.040
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes.

asr-000196
00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:13.540
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: We note that said amount is part of the continuing appropriation for the project released in 2023.

asr-000197
00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:20.340
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: At that time, PCC requested for the issuance of SARO amounting 104 million only.

asr-000198
00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:24.940
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Equivalent to the loan proceeds downloaded by ADB, however,

asr-000199
00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.700
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: DBM issued 280 million instead.

asr-000200
00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:30.840
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Which resulted to the excess resources.

asr-000201
00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:33.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000202
00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:41.620
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: ADB's project data showed that as of June 23, 2026,

asr-000203
00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:50.300
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: cumulative contract awards were only 45% and cumulative loan disbursements were 41%

asr-000204
00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:54.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the loan has now been extended to June 30, 2028.

asr-000205
00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:58.820
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Those figures are not identical to COA's

asr-000206
00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:03.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: fiscal year 2024 utilization ratios

asr-000207
00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:11.480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: but they still indicate that the substantial portion of the project financing remained undisbursed.

asr-000208
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Before Congress provides additional appropriation,

asr-000209
00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:22.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: can the PCC give us its quarterly obligation and disbursement target for fiscal year 2027

asr-000210
00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:28.280
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and identify exactly what activities will absorb these funds.

asr-000211
00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:42.680
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC can point to the loan extension, revised procurement, programming, additional project proposals, and strengthened monitoring as measures intended to accelerate implementation.

asr-000212
00:19:46.210 --> 00:20:01.450
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker. And for my last question, how many pending antitrust or pending cases have been filed or are being reviewed by the Philippine Competition Commission?

asr-000213
00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:24.950
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: There are seven active cases ongoing, Your Honor.

asr-000213-split-2
00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:37.930
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Can we divulge what those seven are, or will it be against the PCC's confidentiality clause?

asr-000213-split-3
00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:43.620
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: We will submit the complete data to you, Your Honor, for you to review.

asr-000214
00:20:43.870 --> 00:21:12.660
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Okay. Thank you. Because, Mr. Speaker, distinguished sponsor, you know the Philippine Competition Commission plays a big role, especially to those merging companies, no, para hindi ho tayo maiwanan sa ere at walang collusion, especially po pagdating sa fuel. As you know, malaki ang problema natin sa fuel ngayon, and I hope the PCC will take cognizance when it comes to energy sources. Again,

asr-000215
00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:23.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you very much, Mr. Speaker, and I always [unclear] for your budget for PCC for this year. Thank you very much.

asr-000216
00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:27.760
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: Thank you, Honorable De Jesus, Majority Leader.

asr-000217
00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:34.080
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Robert Nazal for his interpellation.

asr-000218
00:21:34.800 --> 00:21:39.620
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: The Honorable Robert Nazal of Partylist BH is recognized. Please proceed.

asr-000219
00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:42.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Good evening, Mr. Chair.

asr-000220
00:21:42.680 --> 00:21:59.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, may I ask the PCC, have you studied what happens when a major retailer is both the gatekeeper of the market and a competitor of suppliers selling inside its stores?

asr-000221
00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:02.140
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes.

asr-000223
00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:07.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Pinag-aaralan niyo po yan.

asr-000224
00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:08.100
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes.

asr-000225
00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:12.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Major retailers carry products made by independent suppliers.

asr-000226
00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:17.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But they may also develop their own private label products.

asr-000227
00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:23.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Sometimes products very similar to those already being successfully sold by their suppliers.

asr-000228
00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:28.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So there is nothing inherently illegal about private labels.

asr-000229
00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:42.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But the retailer knows what sells, controls the shelf, and counter space, controls inventory and promotions,

asr-000230
00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:47.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and then competes against the supplier with its own product.

asr-000231
00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:48.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Nangyayari po ito.

asr-000232
00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:53.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: At what point does this become a competition concern?

asr-000233
00:22:54.060 --> 00:22:55.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Or when does it become?

asr-000234
00:22:56.180 --> 00:23:00.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Inaanalyze po ba natin when it becomes predatory in practice?

asr-000240
00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:31.560
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC is closely monitoring that's happening and a thorough investigation will be conducted.

asr-000241
00:23:32.040 --> 00:23:42.360
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Meron na po ba kayong nakitang mga ganito? And were there complaints, for example, that were filed with the PCC that was actually investigated upon?

asr-000242
00:23:42.680 --> 00:23:43.600
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: There were minor complaints.

asr-000243
00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:51.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what intervention, Mr. Chair and distinguished colleague, ang ginawa po ng PCC?

asr-000244
00:23:52.340 --> 00:24:03.160
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: There were minor complaints but it was given an attention and it was informed to the manufacturer.

asr-000245
00:24:04.600 --> 00:24:09.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, meron po ba tayong portal na pwedeng magreklamo ang, let's say, SMEs?

asr-000246
00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:12.440
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: We can use the website.

asr-000247
00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:16.200
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Of the PCC and the social media.

asr-000248
00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:32.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And is it very easy to file a complaint? And once an SME, for example, files a complaint against any predatory practice, ganong katagal ang response time?

asr-000249
00:24:35.100 --> 00:24:42.500
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes, pwedeng madali ang mag-file ng complaint kasi pwede sa online at sa Facebook page ng PCC.

asr-000250
00:24:42.680 --> 00:24:46.720
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Kaya ganon, kadali ang pag-file, may investigation kagad.

asr-000251
00:24:47.440 --> 00:24:51.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Chair, distinguished colleague, let me give a practical example.

asr-000252
00:24:52.500 --> 00:25:00.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung may independent brand na successful, then the retailer comes out with a very similar own brand product at a lower price.

asr-000253
00:25:02.100 --> 00:25:07.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Tapos yung sariling brand niya, prominently displayed and readily available sa counter.

asr-000254
00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:11.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: While yung competing product, wala doon, kailangan magbayad.

asr-000255
00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:15.640
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Tapos yung staff, kailangan pang umalas para kunin.

asr-000256
00:25:16.460 --> 00:25:19.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The retailer controls both the competition and the playing field.

asr-000257
00:25:20.820 --> 00:25:23.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Does the PCC examine practices like this?

asr-000258
00:25:27.300 --> 00:25:28.440
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes, yes.

asr-000259
00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:35.020
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: That's called self-preferencing.

asr-000260
00:25:36.180 --> 00:25:41.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And ano pong actions ang pwede natin gawin in case meron tayong nahuhuling ganito?

asr-000261
00:25:42.680 --> 00:25:52.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What intervention can the PCC do in behalf of those experiencing predatory practices?

asr-000262
00:25:52.500 --> 00:25:59.180
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC can file a case against the retailer.

asr-000263
00:26:00.420 --> 00:26:03.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What if the retailer po is a giant?

asr-000264
00:26:11.060 --> 00:26:12.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Malakas, ha?

asr-000265
00:26:12.680 --> 00:26:19.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And pwede po niyang balikan kasi yung halimbawa, pwede niyang balikan yung SME.

asr-000266
00:26:19.020 --> 00:26:27.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And if there are only a few retailers in the country, paano po ang mangyayari kung ang gagawin niya,

asr-000267
00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:33.280
Rep. Roberto Nazal: ang magiging balik niya doon sa nagreklamo, ay ibabanan niya sa shelf?

asr-000268
00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:41.900
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: The PCC is mandated. May mandato ang PCC na kahit malaking tao man lang, kahit gaano kalaki, pwedeng sagasaan.

asr-000269
00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:42.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And the PCC?

asr-000270
00:26:42.500 --> 00:26:47.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The PCC guarantees that it can protect small players against practices such as this.

asr-000271
00:26:48.440 --> 00:26:48.800
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Definitely.

asr-000272
00:26:48.800 --> 00:26:52.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Mr. Chair, distinguished sponsor.

asr-000273
00:26:54.180 --> 00:27:05.820
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Chair, has PCC ever conducted a market study comparing how major retailers treat their own private label products versus competing independent brands?

asr-000274
00:27:07.080 --> 00:27:10.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: In shelf and counter placement, inventory availability,

asr-000275
00:27:11.620 --> 00:27:11.880
Rep. Roberto Nazal: promotion,

asr-000276
00:27:12.500 --> 00:27:15.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: access to sales data,

asr-000277
00:27:15.920 --> 00:27:16.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: pricing,

asr-000278
00:27:16.900 --> 00:27:17.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: supplier fees,

asr-000279
00:27:17.880 --> 00:27:18.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: payment terms,

asr-000280
00:27:18.620 --> 00:27:19.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and other conditions.

asr-000281
00:27:20.600 --> 00:27:25.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Because ang concern po natin is not simply that they copied the product or made something cheaper.

asr-000282
00:27:26.240 --> 00:27:33.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The concern is whether a powerful retailer can identify a successful product from one of its suppliers,

asr-000283
00:27:34.800 --> 00:27:36.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: introduce its own competing version,

asr-000284
00:27:36.580 --> 00:27:42.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and then use its control of the retail channel to give its own product.

asr-000285
00:27:42.500 --> 00:27:47.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: An unfair advantage, and eventually squeeze the independent supplier out.

asr-000286
00:27:48.260 --> 00:27:53.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Does our present competition framework adequately protect against that?

asr-000287
00:27:53.040 --> 00:27:54.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you very much.

asr-000288
00:27:57.240 --> 00:28:08.880
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Wala pang public study, but we had compelled a very big retailer to be fair.

asr-000289
00:28:10.640 --> 00:28:12.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So ano pong kailangan na?

asr-000290
00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:18.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Is there anything you need, for example, from Congress in terms of amending your charter, strengthening it?

asr-000291
00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:29.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Meron po ba tayo naiisip na mga pwede natin baguhin para po palakasin at bigyan ng pangil ang Philippine Competition Commission

asr-000292
00:28:29.300 --> 00:28:35.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: para po lalo natin maprotektahan ang ating mga maliliit na nag-uumpisang maghanap buhay?

asr-000297
00:28:39.180 --> 00:28:42.180
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: There is a pending bill on the committee.

asr-000298
00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:45.680
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: On economic affairs, I think.

asr-000299
00:28:46.180 --> 00:28:50.280
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: And the PCC is closely working with the committee.

asr-000300
00:28:51.120 --> 00:28:56.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I would like to co-author that, Mr. Chair, and the distinguished sponsor.

asr-000301
00:28:56.920 --> 00:29:03.000
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Chair, is PCC looking at the same gatekeeper problem in online platforms

asr-000302
00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:09.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: where the operator of the marketplace may also sell or promote products that compete with merchants

asr-000303
00:29:09.500 --> 00:29:12.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: dependent on that marketplace?

asr-000304
00:29:12.200 --> 00:29:19.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What safeguards does PCC consider necessary when the platform or retailer controls both

asr-000305
00:29:19.200 --> 00:29:22.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: access to customer and the competitive environment?

asr-000306
00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:29.200
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Para sa online naman po ito, distinguished sponsor.

asr-000307
00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:34.200
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes, we are looking to it.

asr-000308
00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:38.930
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: And in terms of safeguarding the…

asr-000318
00:29:51.970 --> 00:29:54.450
Rep. Roberto Nazal: [unclear]

asr-000323
00:30:02.350 --> 00:30:17.860
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: We are closely monitoring the market, and if there is a violation, we are bound to file a complaint.

asr-000324
00:30:18.010 --> 00:30:34.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kaya ako po tinatanong ito, Distinguished Sponsor, Mr. Speaker. Kasi po, ang napansin ko, noon, lalo na nung pandemic, naging advantage po ngayon yung online retailers.

asr-000325
00:30:34.140 --> 00:30:46.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So yung online platforms were helping yung ating maliliit na negosyante. Parang ang lumalabas ngayon, yung ating mga retailers, giant retailers,

asr-000326
00:30:46.160 --> 00:30:56.420
Rep. Roberto Nazal: tsaka yung online at digital platforms are already charging, if not the same, yung ating digital platforms are charging even more.

asr-000327
00:30:57.620 --> 00:31:03.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And ang gusto ko po sanang alamin is kung natitignan po natin yung charges na sinisingil nila.

asr-000328
00:31:03.220 --> 00:31:14.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi if you will ask and do conduct a study or maybe an online survey, tanungin nyo po yung mga nagbibenta online.

asr-000329
00:31:14.680 --> 00:31:20.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: The digital platforms are now charging maybe up to 60%.

asr-000330
00:31:20.060 --> 00:31:28.460
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And parang ang nangyayari, kung 100 pesos yung binibenta mo, 60 pesos na yung kinukuha nila, minsan 70 pesos pa.

asr-000331
00:31:29.200 --> 00:31:32.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So ang matitira sa'yo, 30 pesos, kukunin mo pa dun yung cost mo.

asr-000332
00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:43.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So my concern is the PCC looking into that. Kasi po, dapat ho, I think it's about time that we monitor this.

asr-000333
00:31:43.020 --> 00:31:45.620
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi kung ano-anong charges ang nilalagay nila.

asr-000334
00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:56.020
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: We have looked into the digital platforms but not into that specific issue but we will see it now.

asr-000335
00:31:56.340 --> 00:31:57.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000336
00:31:58.740 --> 00:32:12.960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Chair, Distinguished Sponsor, have you also studied the competition implications when a conglomerate owns both a bank and businesses in sectors heavily dependent on financing such as real estate?

asr-000337
00:32:13.020 --> 00:32:26.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Even if related party lending complies with banking regulations, can preferential access to financing reinforce market power in the conglomerate's non-banking business?

asr-000338
00:32:26.980 --> 00:32:31.380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And has PCC studied this as a structural competition issue?

asr-000339
00:32:35.940 --> 00:32:42.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Ang tinatanong ko po ay yung possible whether PCC studies cross-sector competitive effects.

asr-000340
00:32:43.020 --> 00:32:45.260
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes, we have.

asr-000341
00:32:45.860 --> 00:32:47.980
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So you're already looking into that, Mr. Chair?

asr-000342
00:32:49.300 --> 00:32:51.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Distinguished Sponsor, the PCC?

asr-000343
00:32:51.540 --> 00:32:52.180
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes, we have.

asr-000344
00:32:53.180 --> 00:32:59.800
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So meron na po ba kayong nakita na, for example, industry na because of this, nagkakaroon ng unfair advantage?

asr-000345
00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:09.140
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And if this is so, what is the, ano po ang gagawin ng PCC in order to help level the playing field?

asr-000346
00:33:13.020 --> 00:33:20.900
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: So far, wala pang nakikitang ganyan. Pero pag meron, rest assured na maaksyonan kagalit.

asr-000347
00:33:20.900 --> 00:33:28.680
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So baka po pwede natin tignan, maybe we can use AI to look into this kung ano po yung mga possible effects.

asr-000348
00:33:28.800 --> 00:33:31.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi siyempre, magkakaroon po ng unfair advantage, di ba?

asr-000349
00:33:34.100 --> 00:33:42.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Mr. Chair, Mr. Chair, Distinguished Colleague, the PCC's proposed 2027 budget is approximately 832 million.

asr-000350
00:33:43.020 --> 00:33:47.460
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Including funding for competition, capacity building.

asr-000351
00:33:48.900 --> 00:33:54.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: What concrete sector reviews and enforcement milestones will this funding deliver?

asr-000352
00:33:55.060 --> 00:34:01.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Particularly for retail, digital platforms, and other highly concentrated markets.

asr-000353
00:34:01.780 --> 00:34:10.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Will the PCC use its own investigative authority proactively rather than require small businesses to initiate every case?

asr-000354
00:34:10.600 --> 00:34:12.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So ang tinatanong po natin is,

asr-000355
00:34:13.020 --> 00:34:20.320
Rep. Roberto Nazal: mag-aantay pa po ba tayo ng mga complaint bago tayong makagalaw?

asr-000356
00:34:20.420 --> 00:34:25.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Or will we proactively seek measures which will protect small businesses?

asr-000357
00:34:37.860 --> 00:34:42.420
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: We actively monitor the social medias.

asr-000358
00:34:43.020 --> 00:34:49.180
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: And any complaint, and we will immediately act on this matter.

asr-000359
00:34:49.540 --> 00:34:52.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: May I request for a plan?

asr-000360
00:34:52.920 --> 00:34:57.260
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kung ano, how do you intend to spend the 832 million?

asr-000361
00:34:57.860 --> 00:35:07.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And ano po yung safeguards na pwede na, safeguards that you plan to impose?

asr-000362
00:35:07.020 --> 00:35:10.740
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Plan sector studies, measurable outputs.

asr-000363
00:35:11.860 --> 00:35:12.860
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And how SMEs?

asr-000364
00:35:13.020 --> 00:35:18.900
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And suppliers can safely provide market information without fear of commercial retaliation?

asr-000365
00:35:20.540 --> 00:35:22.680
Rep. Dante S. Garcia: Yes, Your Honor, we will provide you a copy.

asr-000366
00:35:28.500 --> 00:35:34.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, I'm, that's all for all, para sa mga tanong ko.

asr-000367
00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:35.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Maraming salamat sa PCC.

asr-000368
00:35:35.920 --> 00:35:42.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And I hope the PCC will proactively craft,

asr-000369
00:35:43.020 --> 00:35:51.380
Rep. Roberto Nazal: proactively craft measures na makakatulong po at makakaprotekta po sa ating maliliit na naghahanap buhay.

asr-000370
00:35:51.540 --> 00:35:52.260
