asr-000901
00:56:01.020 --> 00:56:09.020
Rep. Rhea Mae A. Gullas: Mr. Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Presley De Jesus for his interpellation.

asr-000902
00:56:09.580 --> 00:56:14.340
Deputy Speaker Ferjenel G. Biron, M.D.: The Honorable Presley De Jesus of Partilis, Felrica is recognized. Please proceed.

asr-000903
00:56:14.840 --> 00:56:17.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, good evening.

asr-000904
00:56:18.600 --> 00:56:28.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Earlier this year, DBM issued Corporate Budget Memorandum No. 48 for the Fiscal Year 2027 Corporate Budget Call.

asr-000905
00:56:28.980 --> 00:56:31.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Under the policy, it was stated that the DBM should not be involved in corporate budget calls.

asr-000906
00:56:31.020 --> 00:56:51.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Under the policy, it was stated that a GOCC receiving 60% or more its funding from national government subsidies for the past 10 consecutive years is automatically flagged for mandatory institutional review for GOCCs covered by Republic Act No. 10149.

asr-000907
00:56:51.640 --> 00:56:58.400
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: That review is to be conducted by GCG. Is this correct, Mr. Speaker, Madam Sponsor?

asr-000908
00:56:59.180 --> 00:57:00.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000909
00:57:01.020 --> 00:57:15.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And my follow-up question, then under those parameters, how many GOCCs under GCG's jurisdiction currently meet the 60% subsidy for 10 years threshold?

asr-000910
00:57:19.280 --> 00:57:22.380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The study is ongoing regarding the number, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000911
00:57:22.380 --> 00:57:26.380
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Are we talking about 2026?

asr-000912
00:57:28.980 --> 00:57:30.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Or 2025, I mean? I'm sorry.

asr-000914
00:57:50.740 --> 00:57:55.758
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The GCG is just checking their records, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000916
00:58:01.462 --> 00:58:01.833
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: ...

asr-000917
00:58:31.020 --> 00:58:44.380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: The GCG will just submit the list of GOCCs that satisfy their requirement, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000918
00:58:44.520 --> 00:58:46.240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: That's okay with my distinguished colleague.

asr-000919
00:58:47.460 --> 00:58:49.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Fair enough, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000920
00:58:49.480 --> 00:58:50.720
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I gladly accept that.

asr-000921
00:58:51.700 --> 00:58:53.160
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: My next question,

asr-000922
00:58:55.680 --> 00:59:01.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: have institutional reviews which are now mandated already commenced?

asr-000923
00:59:01.020 --> 00:59:03.240
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: For every one of those GOCCs.

asr-000924
00:59:03.700 --> 00:59:07.140
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: If not, what the timetables are we looking at?

asr-000925
00:59:31.020 --> 00:59:39.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Regarding the monitoring and evaluation of GOCCs, Mr. Speaker, the GCG currently conducts three.

asr-000926
00:59:40.500 --> 00:59:41.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, three.

asr-000927
00:59:42.040 --> 00:59:48.840
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: There's the performance evaluation system for GOCCs, and then there's the performance evaluation for directors in the GOCC sector.

asr-000928
00:59:49.440 --> 00:59:54.020
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And then the GCG also produces corporate governance scorecards.

asr-000929
00:59:54.020 --> 00:59:59.940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: But as per the finalization of the reports for fiscal year 2020,

asr-000930
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:06.580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the GCG is dependent on the submission of COA financial statement.

asr-000931
01:00:07.220 --> 01:00:10.720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So as of now, review is still currently ongoing, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000932
01:00:10.860 --> 01:00:15.480
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So do we expect that later this year or it's going to be next year?

asr-000933
01:00:16.300 --> 01:00:17.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, later in this year, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000934
01:00:18.360 --> 01:00:21.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How many directors are, as you mentioned, that under review?

asr-000935
01:00:22.240 --> 01:00:22.860
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How many of them?

asr-000936
01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:54.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: For, Mr. Speaker, for clarification, director, total directors for all the GOCCs that are being reviewed, total.

asr-000937
01:00:57.540 --> 01:00:59.820
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: We're pulling up the actual number.

asr-000940
01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:03.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So estimated around, approximately around 500 directors, Mr. Speaker.

asr-000941
01:01:04.420 --> 01:01:06.800
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor.

asr-000942
01:01:10.240 --> 01:01:21.200
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Sponsor, could the good sponsor provide the following information for the consideration of this body?

asr-000943
01:01:21.680 --> 01:01:29.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The amount of national government support received by these GOCCs during the past 10 years, its performance, scorecard results,

asr-000944
01:01:29.940 --> 01:01:34.100
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: and the current status of GCG's institutional review.

asr-000945
01:01:36.600 --> 01:01:46.940
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: It's important because the new DBM policy says they are now subject to mandatory institutional review to be conducted by GCG.

asr-000946
01:01:48.380 --> 01:01:52.080
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Kasi po, meron na pong DBM policy na bago ngayon.

asr-000947
01:01:53.080 --> 01:01:58.080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Mr. Speaker, just to clarify, the first would be the amount of government support received by the GOCCs.

asr-000948
01:01:58.080 --> 01:02:01.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: What's the second one, Mr. Speaker?

asr-000949
01:02:02.440 --> 01:02:08.060
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: No, that's the question because I'm just interjecting that there's a new DBM policy.

asr-000950
01:02:09.160 --> 01:02:16.520
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Now, they have to be subjected for mandatory institutional review to be conducted by GCG.

asr-000951
01:02:16.520 --> 01:02:21.720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, sir. Government support.

asr-000952
01:02:21.720 --> 01:02:28.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, sir. Government support.

asr-000954
01:02:38.220 --> 01:02:43.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, the GCG is just pulling up the actual number.

asr-000955
01:02:43.540 --> 01:02:48.380
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: However, just an overall observation regarding the amount of government support,

asr-000956
01:02:48.600 --> 01:02:56.940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it's been declining given that those GOCCs that previously needed government support are now improving in performance.

asr-000957
