05:47:24.000 --> 05:47:26.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, I understand.

asr-005208
05:47:26.000 --> 05:47:31.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I understand this is a policy question that goes beyond the SBMA.

asr-005209
05:47:31.900 --> 05:47:33.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: National issue na po ito.

asr-005210
05:47:33.880 --> 05:47:42.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ang punto po natin ay tumataya ang Marcos Jr. Administration sa Paxilica na ito.

asr-005211
05:47:42.520 --> 05:47:45.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi, the whole Luzon Economic Corridor.

asr-005212
05:47:45.860 --> 05:47:54.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, not just Subic, but also Clark, pati yung sa Batangas, at iba pa na involved sa corridor na yan.

asr-005213
05:47:54.320 --> 05:47:54.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bataan.

asr-005214
05:47:54.960 --> 05:47:57.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nakikita ko ang kasamahan natin from Bataan.

asr-005215
05:47:58.920 --> 05:48:00.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Damay po kayo dyan.

asr-005216
05:48:00.340 --> 05:48:01.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Damay tayong lahat dyan.

asr-005217
05:48:02.800 --> 05:48:11.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And if ever matuloy yung gera na pinag-aandaan ng US laban sa China,

asr-005218
05:48:12.000 --> 05:48:16.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang nakataya po ay ang malaking bahagi ng ating ekonomiya.

asr-005219
05:48:16.920 --> 05:48:24.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kung sakaling mangyari yung nangyari sa Gulf states,

asr-005220
05:48:24.960 --> 05:48:29.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ay babalik po tayo sa parang, in effect, parang pinatubo.

asr-005221
05:48:29.960 --> 05:48:37.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung ano yung nangyari sa Subic at Clark nung panahon ng pinatubo.

asr-005222
05:48:37.900 --> 05:48:38.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, ganun na po.

asr-005223
05:48:38.540 --> 05:48:40.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sagutin ko na sa inyo, anong mangyari dyan?

asr-005224
05:48:40.320 --> 05:48:41.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang pinatubo.

asr-005225
05:48:42.120 --> 05:48:46.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, that would set us back by practically two generations.

asr-005226
05:48:47.000 --> 05:48:48.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung sakaling mangyari po yun.

asr-005227
05:48:48.800 --> 05:48:54.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, the point here, Madam Speaker, is really to question,

asr-005228
05:48:54.960 --> 05:49:04.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the wisdom of this administration in betting on the so-called Pax Silitka

asr-005229
05:49:04.140 --> 05:49:10.940
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: na ang bantapo ay sa pinaka-siguridad ng buhay ng mga Pilipino

asr-005230
05:49:10.940 --> 05:49:17.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at sa ekonomiya mismo at pag-unlad ng Pilipinas.

asr-005231
05:49:17.740 --> 05:49:24.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nang walang anumang pag-iisip at pag-aanda para sa depensa.

asr-005232
05:49:25.120 --> 05:49:25.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba?

asr-005233
05:49:26.080 --> 05:49:31.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya po, with that, Madam Speaker, tatapusin ko na po ang aking interpellation.

asr-005234
05:49:31.260 --> 05:49:32.120
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Maraming salamat po.

asr-005235
05:49:32.460 --> 05:49:33.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No to Pax Silica

asr-005236
05:49:34.780 --> 05:49:37.660
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Do we hear the motion to terminate?

asr-005237
05:49:39.980 --> 05:49:42.020
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Madam Speaker, on the part of the minority.

asr-005238
05:49:43.500 --> 05:49:46.080
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The Honorable Tino, please proceed.

asr-005239
05:49:46.260 --> 05:49:47.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, yes. Okay.

asr-005240
05:49:47.840 --> 05:49:54.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Madam Speaker, there being no other member of the minority who wishes to interpolate,

asr-005241
05:49:54.960 --> 05:50:03.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I move to terminate the period of interpolation and debate on the proposed budget of the SBMA.

asr-005242
