Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: The presentation of the Hon. Tino.

asr-005271
05:52:27.020 --> 05:52:29.300
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: But prior to that, the Hon. Tino can...

asr-005272
05:52:29.300 --> 05:52:30.760
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: There it is.

asr-005273
05:52:31.740 --> 05:52:32.420
Deputy Speaker Janette L. Garin: Okay.

asr-005274
05:52:33.320 --> 05:52:38.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Well, ang main question po natin sa budget ng DOST.

asr-005275
05:52:38.620 --> 05:52:45.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Una po, ito po yung budget ng DOST over a 10-year period,

asr-005276
05:52:45.040 --> 05:52:48.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: including the proposed budget for 2027.

asr-005277
05:52:51.020 --> 05:52:52.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Napansin po natin,

asr-005278
05:52:52.380 --> 05:52:55.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ang tinakamalaking bahagi ng budget.

asr-005279
05:52:55.360 --> 05:52:56.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, for example,

asr-005280
05:52:57.700 --> 05:53:02.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the current proposed budget...

asr-005281
05:53:22.380 --> 05:53:35.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, the proposed budget for 2027 of the DOST is 6.868 Trillion Pesos.

asr-005282
05:53:37.160 --> 05:53:39.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang napansin lang po natin, of that,

asr-005283
05:53:41.340 --> 05:53:44.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: if you look at the breakdown of that budget,

asr-005284
05:53:46.480 --> 05:53:51.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: most of it is in the form of

asr-005285
05:53:51.200 --> 05:53:57.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: financial assistance and subsidy.

asr-005286
05:53:57.280 --> 05:54:02.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of the 6.8 billion,

asr-005287
05:54:02.920 --> 05:54:09.620
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 4.687 billion is listed under financial assistance or subsidy.

asr-005288
05:54:12.160 --> 05:54:17.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, yung chart po na yan,

asr-005289
05:54:17.460 --> 05:54:20.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: pinapakita yung paglaki

asr-005290
05:54:20.060 --> 05:54:21.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng DOST.

asr-005291
05:54:21.200 --> 05:54:24.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang budget, pero ang kalakhang bahagi talaga,

asr-005292
05:54:24.440 --> 05:54:25.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the blue portion,

asr-005293
05:54:26.360 --> 05:54:28.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: is financial assistance and subsidy.

asr-005294
05:54:29.520 --> 05:54:32.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Then, I look at the special provisions.

asr-005295
05:54:32.980 --> 05:54:36.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Usually, pagka may financial assistance and subsidy,

asr-005296
05:54:36.160 --> 05:54:38.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: there should be a special provision

asr-005297
05:54:38.260 --> 05:54:45.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: that lays down the parameters

asr-005298
05:54:45.760 --> 05:54:48.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: on the use of financial assistance and subsidy.

asr-005299
05:54:48.700 --> 05:54:49.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero wala po tayong nakikita.

asr-005300
05:54:49.980 --> 05:54:56.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sa special provisions ng DOST budget ay,

asr-005301
05:54:56.980 --> 05:55:00.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: well, there is mention of a priority research program

asr-005302
05:55:00.980 --> 05:55:02.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and then reporting and posting requirements.

asr-005303
05:55:02.980 --> 05:55:06.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pwede lang po ba malinaw,

asr-005304
05:55:06.980 --> 05:55:11.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: bakit po yung napakalaking bahagi ng inyong budget

asr-005305
05:55:11.980 --> 05:55:15.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: over, let's say, 80% of your budget,

asr-005306
05:55:15.980 --> 05:55:18.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: from eyeballing the charts,

asr-005307
05:55:18.980 --> 05:55:23.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: falls under financial assistance slash subsidy.

asr-005308
05:55:23.980 --> 05:55:26.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Parang ang dating, actually, usually,

asr-005309
05:55:26.980 --> 05:55:29.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yan yung terminong ginagamit sa ayuda.

asr-005310
05:55:29.980 --> 05:55:30.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba?

asr-005311
05:55:30.980 --> 05:55:31.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang mga scholarship.

asr-005312
05:55:31.980 --> 05:55:33.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Bakit po ganun?

asr-005313
05:55:33.980 --> 05:55:36.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague,

asr-005314
05:55:36.980 --> 05:55:37.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: grants and aids po yan.

asr-005315
05:55:37.980 --> 05:55:38.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sorry?

asr-005316
05:55:38.980 --> 05:55:40.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Grants and aids.

asr-005317
05:55:40.980 --> 05:55:42.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, yun. Grants and aids.

asr-005318
05:55:42.980 --> 05:55:43.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005319
05:55:43.980 --> 05:55:47.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, all of the,

asr-005320
05:55:47.980 --> 05:55:51.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: grants and aids are under the Office of the Secretary.

asr-005321
05:55:51.980 --> 05:55:53.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Highly centralized po yung budget.

asr-005322
05:55:53.980 --> 05:56:00.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya po tinatawag na financial subsidy ay dahil sa,

asr-005323
05:56:00.980 --> 05:56:02.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ito ay mga grants and aids.

asr-005324
05:56:02.980 --> 05:56:07.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ano po mga example ng grants and aids na ito?

asr-005325
05:56:07.980 --> 05:56:09.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At pwede po bang,

asr-005326
05:56:09.980 --> 05:56:13.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yan lang, mabigyan tayo ng breakdown ng grants and aids?

asr-005327
05:56:13.980 --> 05:56:15.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Ah, yes.

asr-005328
05:56:15.980 --> 05:56:16.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Madam Speaker,

asr-005329
05:56:16.980 --> 05:56:17.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Madam Speaker,

asr-005330
05:56:17.980 --> 05:56:19.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: ah, distinguished colleague,

asr-005331
05:56:19.980 --> 05:56:20.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: ah,

asr-005332
05:56:20.980 --> 05:56:21.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: first,

asr-005333
05:56:21.980 --> 05:56:25.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: ah, napupunta po ito sa research and development,

asr-005334
05:56:25.980 --> 05:56:27.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: or R&amp;D,

asr-005335
05:56:27.980 --> 05:56:29.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: ah,

asr-005336
05:56:29.980 --> 05:56:31.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: CEST,

asr-005337
05:56:31.980 --> 05:56:33.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: ah, setup,

asr-005338
05:56:33.980 --> 05:56:36.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: at ah, smart and sustainable community,

asr-005339
05:56:36.980 --> 05:56:40.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: and ah, last is, ah, tax transfer.

asr-005340
05:56:40.980 --> 05:56:42.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005341
05:56:42.980 --> 05:56:44.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah,

asr-005342
05:56:44.980 --> 05:56:46.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sige, baka pwede po magma,

asr-005343
05:56:46.980 --> 05:56:51.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: makapag-provide na lang ng, ah, breakdown nitong mga grants and aids

asr-005344
05:56:51.980 --> 05:56:54.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: for 2026 and the proposed grants and aid,

asr-005345
05:56:54.980 --> 05:56:59.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: grants and aid for 2027.

asr-005346
05:56:59.980 --> 05:57:00.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay po ba yun?

asr-005347
05:57:00.980 --> 05:57:02.980
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Yes, of course, ah.

asr-005348
05:57:02.980 --> 05:57:03.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, thank you po.

asr-005349
05:57:03.980 --> 05:57:04.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Singis gulit.

asr-005350
05:57:04.980 --> 05:57:07.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ah, ngayon, during the budget briefings, ah,

asr-005351
05:57:07.980 --> 05:57:12.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: isa po sa mga nakita natin at medyo nagtanong tayo ng konti ay tungkol sa, ah, plano ng DOL, ah,

asr-005352
05:57:12.980 --> 05:57:16.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: plano ng DOST para sa AI.

asr-005353
05:57:16.980 --> 05:57:17.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

asr-005354
05:57:17.980 --> 05:57:21.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And the concept of, ah, AI sovereignty.

asr-005355
05:57:21.980 --> 05:57:22.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

asr-005356
05:57:22.980 --> 05:57:23.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005357
05:57:23.980 --> 05:57:28.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pwede po bang mapaliwanag ng, ah, sponsor,

asr-005358
05:57:28.980 --> 05:57:34.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ano yung plano ng DOST kaugnay dito sa development ng AI sovereignty

asr-005359
05:57:34.980 --> 05:57:41.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at magkano po yung, ah, ginamit na, nagastos na, at gagastusin in the proposed budget

asr-005360
05:57:41.980 --> 05:57:43.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: to develop AI sovereignty?

asr-005361
05:57:43.980 --> 05:57:46.980
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano ba tong AI sovereignty in the first place?

asr-005364
05:58:05.980 --> 05:58:14.160
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

asr-005365
05:58:14.320 --> 05:58:20.080
Rep. Amben S. Amante: ang isa po sa mga dine-develop po ng DOST ngayon ay yung Research Data Center.

asr-005366
05:58:20.080 --> 05:58:39.000
Rep. Amben S. Amante: And also data digital transformation to fuel AI.

asr-005367
05:58:39.000 --> 05:58:46.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Pero tama po. So, Research in AI.

asr-005368
05:58:48.760 --> 05:58:49.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero yung konsepto nga.

asr-005369
05:58:50.080 --> 05:58:57.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang DOST kaugnay ng AI sovereignty. Parang meron pong ginagawa ang DOST kaugnay niyan.

asr-005370
05:58:57.980 --> 05:59:05.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ba yun? What does that mean? AI sovereignty at anong ginagawa ng DOST tungo rito?

asr-005371
05:59:12.600 --> 05:59:13.480
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Thank you.

asr-005372
05:59:15.480 --> 05:59:19.560
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, the DOST-ASDI,

asr-005373
05:59:20.080 --> 05:59:27.240
Rep. Amben S. Amante: currently has the facilities for Research Data Center, Cloud Computing, and HPC.

asr-005374
05:59:27.240 --> 05:59:39.540
Rep. Amben S. Amante: At an average of operational utilization at 33%, consisting of 38 storage servers, 22 compute servers,

asr-005375
05:59:39.800 --> 05:59:49.880
Rep. Amben S. Amante: and 10 GPU servers to ensure operational and services that AI infrastructure is currently being set up in a data center.

asr-005376
05:59:49.880 --> 05:59:57.620
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Within Metro Manila, within 24 H200 GPUs at 1248 CPU cores.

asr-005377
06:00:00.180 --> 06:00:03.860
Rep. Amben S. Amante: 11,264 gigabytes RAM,

asr-005378
06:00:04.060 --> 06:00:11.720
Rep. Amben S. Amante: and 1,574 terabytes storage.

asr-005379
06:00:12.860 --> 06:00:15.960
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Well, thank you for that detailed answer.

asr-005380
06:00:16.440 --> 06:00:22.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kung pwede po, mahingi ko yung return para mabalikan natin. Maraming information po yung binibigay nyo.

asr-005381
06:00:22.380 --> 06:00:28.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, sa isensya ang sinasabi nyo po, dito sa Metro Manila, meti na yung data center.

asr-005382
06:00:28.100 --> 06:00:33.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: AI data center ang DOST na merong sariling kapasidad.

asr-005383
06:00:34.540 --> 06:00:43.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung binanggit nyo, how many GPUs yung nandyan, yung capacity, yung storage, and so on and so forth. Tama po?

asr-005384
06:00:44.160 --> 06:00:47.960
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Tama po kayo, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-005385
06:00:47.960 --> 06:00:53.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Ang ibig po sabihin yan, yung AI dito ay nasa Pilipinas.

asr-005386
06:00:53.340 --> 06:01:08.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No? Kasi yung siguro, alam natin, malaganap na ang paggamit ng AI, pero yung karaniwang ginagamit ng mga Pilipino ay nakabase sa ibang bansa yan at pag-aari ng ibang bansa, mainly US, also China.

asr-005387
06:01:09.340 --> 06:01:23.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba? For example, kung gumagamit ng chat GPT, ang mga server, mga computer, mga data center na nagpapatakbo nun ay nasa labas ng Pilipinas, pag-aari ng US.

asr-005388
06:01:23.340 --> 06:01:26.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ng mga kumpanya ng US, pinagkikitaan nila.

asr-005389
06:01:27.300 --> 06:01:28.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganun po, no?

asr-005390
06:01:28.080 --> 06:01:48.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya nga po, mahalaga yung ginagawa ng DOST dahil sinasabi ng marami, magiging importanteng teknolohiya ang AI, importante na may sarili tayong kapasidad sa loob ng bansa para sa AI.

asr-005391
06:01:48.740 --> 06:01:52.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At yung binanggit na data center na pinagkakitaan.

asr-005392
06:01:53.340 --> 06:01:57.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Nagpapatakbo ngayon ng DOST ay bahagi nun, diba?

asr-005393
06:01:58.340 --> 06:02:06.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para kahit maputulan tayo ng access sa AI ng US, meron tayo dito.

asr-005394
06:02:07.340 --> 06:02:09.740
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama? Tama po ba? Ganun po ba?

asr-005395
06:02:09.780 --> 06:02:10.060
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Yes.

asr-005396
06:02:10.760 --> 06:02:11.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005397
06:02:11.400 --> 06:02:12.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Madam Speaker.

asr-005398
06:02:12.180 --> 06:02:13.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alright. Okay.

asr-005399
06:02:13.020 --> 06:02:23.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, makano yung budget na for 2026 na inilaan dyan at para sa 2027?

asr-005400
06:02:23.340 --> 06:02:24.900
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkano ang hinihingi ninyo?

asr-005401
06:02:25.940 --> 06:02:28.340
Rep. Amben S. Amante: For 2027, 300...

asr-005402
06:02:28.860 --> 06:02:30.420
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 2026 po muna. 2026.

asr-005403
06:02:30.560 --> 06:02:36.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Makano na po yung binadjet dyan? Kung meron man. 2026 and then 2027.

asr-005404
06:02:37.940 --> 06:02:40.340
Rep. Amben S. Amante: 200 million, Madam Speaker, this year.

asr-005405
06:02:41.040 --> 06:02:42.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This year, 200 million?

asr-005406
06:02:43.460 --> 06:02:43.740
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Correct.

asr-005407
06:02:44.320 --> 06:02:45.400
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And for next year?

asr-005408
06:02:46.520 --> 06:02:47.680
Rep. Amben S. Amante: 345 million.

asr-005409
06:02:47.680 --> 06:02:51.680
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 345 million as investment in our own...

asr-005410
06:02:53.340 --> 06:02:56.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: AI capacity, kumbaga. Parang ganun.

asr-005411
06:02:56.980 --> 06:02:57.200
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Yes.

asr-005412
06:02:57.240 --> 06:03:02.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tapos yung mga AI model na ginagamit, ano yun? Open source po ba yan? Paano yan?

asr-005413
06:03:04.540 --> 06:03:06.100
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Open source, Madam Speaker.

asr-005414
06:03:06.140 --> 06:03:12.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Open source model. Siyempre, hindi pwedeng gamitin natin yung closed source models, kaya nga closed source eh.

asr-005415
06:03:14.460 --> 06:03:18.860
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Commercially, privately owned ng open AI, anthropic, et cetera.

asr-005416
06:03:19.600 --> 06:03:19.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005417
06:03:19.820 --> 06:03:22.820
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po? If I may ask, ano yung mga...

asr-005418
06:03:23.340 --> 06:03:27.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Open source models na pinagbabataya ng inyong...

asr-005419
06:03:27.240 --> 06:03:29.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ng inyong dine-develop na AI?

asr-005420
06:03:39.260 --> 06:03:42.840
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Mga local large language, Madam Speaker.

asr-005421
06:03:42.840 --> 06:03:47.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes, local large language models, pero these large language models usually may mga...

asr-005422
06:03:48.720 --> 06:03:51.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: may mga kilala eh, na ginagamit.

asr-005423
06:03:52.560 --> 06:03:52.840
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, for example...

asr-005424
06:03:53.340 --> 06:03:57.360
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Lama. Iyan yung ginawa ng Meta, pero open source.

asr-005425
06:03:58.060 --> 06:04:06.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ngayon, actually, ang mga pinaka-mahalagang open source models are the ones developed by Chinese companies, no?

asr-005426
06:04:06.240 --> 06:04:14.060
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Like Quen, Kimi, iyan yung mga ilang open source models.

asr-005427
06:04:14.580 --> 06:04:16.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ano po ang ginagamit ng...

asr-005428
06:04:16.340 --> 06:04:19.820
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Madam Speaker, we are using Opus.

asr-005429
06:04:20.260 --> 06:04:20.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sorry?

asr-005430
06:04:20.940 --> 06:04:21.420
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Opus.

asr-005431
06:04:23.340 --> 06:04:24.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pakiulit po.

asr-005432
06:04:24.360 --> 06:04:24.880
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Opus.

asr-005433
06:04:25.920 --> 06:04:26.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opus.

asr-005434
06:04:26.900 --> 06:04:27.260
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Yes.

asr-005435
06:04:27.740 --> 06:04:28.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opus.

asr-005436
06:04:29.960 --> 06:04:32.780
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Opus, as far as I know, is proprietary.

asr-005437
06:04:33.420 --> 06:04:35.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Claude, hindi po ba? Anthropic po yun, ha?

asr-005438
06:04:46.060 --> 06:04:50.340
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Is it okay, Madam Speaker, na we can send the details to the Office of...

asr-005439
06:04:50.340 --> 06:04:53.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O, sige. Detail na lang po. O, sige. Importante po. Mahalaga.

asr-005440
06:04:53.340 --> 06:04:55.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Magkaroon tayo ng...

asr-005441
06:04:55.460 --> 06:04:57.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: I mean, at least, sige. Huwag na po sa plenaryo.

asr-005442
06:04:58.260 --> 06:05:01.540
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibigay na lang po yung mas technical na detalye kaugnay nito.

asr-005443
06:05:02.000 --> 06:05:02.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005444
06:05:03.000 --> 06:05:09.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, at least, meron pong initiative and effort ng DOST to develop...

asr-005445
06:05:11.160 --> 06:05:15.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Let's call it local AI.

asr-005446
06:05:16.180 --> 06:05:16.380
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

asr-005447
06:05:17.060 --> 06:05:19.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, ibig sabihin nun, kailangan may sarili kang data center

asr-005448
06:05:19.800 --> 06:05:23.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at meron kang sariling large language.

asr-005449
06:05:23.340 --> 06:05:25.180
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Large language models na gagamitin.

asr-005450
06:05:25.820 --> 06:05:26.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005451
06:05:26.960 --> 06:05:30.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Now, let me go to Paxilica again.

asr-005452
06:05:31.660 --> 06:05:35.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Alam natin, as far as we know, hindi directly involved ang DOST dyan.

asr-005453
06:05:35.860 --> 06:05:36.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Tama po ba?

asr-005454
06:05:36.840 --> 06:05:38.400
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Tama po, Madam Speaker.

asr-005455
06:05:38.680 --> 06:05:47.220
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: However, Paxilica, as an initiative, is involved with AI, among others.

asr-005456
06:05:47.920 --> 06:05:48.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-005457
06:05:48.020 --> 06:05:48.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-005458
06:05:50.100 --> 06:05:53.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung AI, advanced AI manufacturing.

asr-005459
06:05:53.340 --> 06:06:03.480
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: And securing the critical mineral supply chain in order to develop AI.

asr-005460
06:06:04.580 --> 06:06:10.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig nila sabihin, yung mga critical minerals to develop the semiconductors,

asr-005461
06:06:10.880 --> 06:06:16.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the advanced GPUs, to be able to run, to develop and run

asr-005462
06:06:16.800 --> 06:06:22.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the most advanced artificial intelligence models.

asr-005463
06:06:22.340 --> 06:06:23.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Models.

asr-005464
06:06:23.580 --> 06:06:23.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005465
06:06:23.940 --> 06:06:30.500
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Dahil ang paniniwala ng US, kung sino ang may pinaka-advancing AI,

asr-005466
06:06:31.360 --> 06:06:37.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: siya ay magkakaroon ng bentahe economically and militarily.

asr-005467
06:06:38.640 --> 06:06:42.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, kaya nagtutunggalian po ang US at China dito.

asr-005468
06:06:42.440 --> 06:06:51.800
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: At ang ginagawa ng US ay pinagkakaitila sa China yung mga pinaka-advanced na AI chips.

asr-005469
06:06:52.200 --> 06:06:52.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Diba?

asr-005470
06:06:52.340 --> 06:07:01.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, these are the export controls imposed by the US on advanced GPUs to China.

asr-005471
06:07:02.180 --> 06:07:10.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ang ganti naman ng China ay pinagkakait nila sa US yung rare earth minerals na kailangan para ma-produce yun.

asr-005472
06:07:10.400 --> 06:07:11.580
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, nandyan po tayo ngayon.

asr-005473
06:07:11.720 --> 06:07:12.720
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kaya may Paxilica.

asr-005474
06:07:13.400 --> 06:07:13.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay.

asr-005475
06:07:13.940 --> 06:07:15.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Why do I mention Paxilica?

asr-005476
06:07:15.520 --> 06:07:19.260
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Because I would like to place on the record,

asr-005477
06:07:19.780 --> 06:07:21.020
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: ah,

asr-005478
06:07:21.540 --> 06:07:22.320
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a recent,

asr-005479
06:07:22.340 --> 06:07:29.760
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a fairly recent speech of the US Undersecretary of State for Economic Affairs,

asr-005480
06:07:29.840 --> 06:07:30.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Jacob Helberg.

asr-005481
06:07:30.900 --> 06:07:33.520
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayan, ilang beses siya nababanggit kanina pa,

asr-005482
06:07:34.200 --> 06:07:37.140
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: dahil siya yung pangunahing arkitekto ng Paxilica,

asr-005483
06:07:37.780 --> 06:07:45.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: at siya mismo yung pumunta dito sa Pilipinas para nga ma-inaugurate yung Paxilica sa New Clark City,

asr-005484
06:07:45.340 --> 06:07:52.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: siya yung nakapirma at counterpart ni BCDA President Bingkang,

asr-005485
06:07:52.340 --> 06:07:54.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: sila yung nagpipirmahan.

asr-005486
06:07:54.340 --> 06:07:56.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito, Jacob Helberg.

asr-005487
06:07:56.340 --> 06:08:02.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, what does he have to say particularly about AI sovereignty or digital sovereignty?

asr-005488
06:08:02.340 --> 06:08:13.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Meron po siyang speech published by the US State Department available on their website.

asr-005489
06:08:13.340 --> 06:08:19.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi ko alam kung may visual tayo dyan, pero it's not really necessary, I can just read it.

asr-005490
06:08:19.340 --> 06:08:21.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This is dated June 25, 2020.

asr-005491
06:08:21.340 --> 06:08:30.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: The title of this speech is the Digital Sovereignty Trap.

asr-005492
06:08:30.340 --> 06:08:31.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ayan.

asr-005493
06:08:31.340 --> 06:08:39.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ganito po, let me read into the record the words of the main architect of Paxilica.

asr-005494
06:08:39.340 --> 06:08:48.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Para alam po ng lahat ano ba ang pag-iisip talaga nung nagtutulak ng Paxilica na niyayakap ng Marcos Jr. Administration.

asr-005495
06:08:48.340 --> 06:08:50.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: These days,

asr-005496
06:08:50.340 --> 06:08:55.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: few words flatter a government like digital sovereignty.

asr-005497
06:08:55.340 --> 06:09:00.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It carries the music of independence, the dignity of self-rule,

asr-005498
06:09:00.340 --> 06:09:04.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the promise that the nation holds its own destiny in its hands.

asr-005499
06:09:04.340 --> 06:09:14.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So it is no surprise that the expression has been pressed into the service of a fashionable, fast-spreading policy debate.

asr-005500
06:09:14.340 --> 06:09:15.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-005501
06:09:15.340 --> 06:09:18.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It is a growing number of governments,

asr-005502
06:09:18.340 --> 06:09:24.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: persuaded that independence requires duplication,

asr-005503
06:09:24.340 --> 06:09:28.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a drafting national AI strategies to match.

asr-005504
06:09:28.340 --> 06:09:36.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Each resolved to rebuild inside its own borders a stack that already exists somewhere else.

asr-005505
06:09:36.340 --> 06:09:38.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun po ang ginagawa ng DOST.

asr-005506
06:09:38.340 --> 06:09:42.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: They are building a domestic AI stack.

asr-005507
06:09:42.340 --> 06:09:43.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Di ba?

asr-005508
06:09:43.340 --> 06:09:45.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yung mga data center,

asr-005509
06:09:45.340 --> 06:09:46.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung equipment,

asr-005510
06:09:46.340 --> 06:09:47.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung hardware,

asr-005511
06:09:47.340 --> 06:09:48.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and also the software,

asr-005512
06:09:48.340 --> 06:09:50.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the large language models,

asr-005513
06:09:50.340 --> 06:09:51.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: open source.

asr-005514
06:09:51.340 --> 06:09:54.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ito yung tinutukoy ni Helberg.

asr-005515
06:09:54.340 --> 06:09:55.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: O.

asr-005516
06:09:55.340 --> 06:09:57.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Kayong mga ibang bansa,

asr-005517
06:09:57.340 --> 06:10:01.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: you are scrambling to develop your own,

asr-005518
06:10:01.340 --> 06:10:03.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: within your own borders,

asr-005519
06:10:03.340 --> 06:10:05.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: your own AI stack.

asr-005520
06:10:05.340 --> 06:10:07.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: What does he have to say about it?

asr-005521
06:10:07.340 --> 06:10:08.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Quote,

asr-005522
06:10:08.340 --> 06:10:10.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It is a seductive vision.

asr-005523
06:10:10.340 --> 06:10:12.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It is a seductive vision.

asr-005524
06:10:12.340 --> 06:10:16.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: It is also backward and counterproductive.

asr-005525
06:10:16.340 --> 06:10:19.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yun ang sabi ni Helberg.

asr-005526
06:10:19.340 --> 06:10:21.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So,

asr-005527
06:10:21.340 --> 06:10:23.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: picture this conference.

asr-005528
06:10:23.340 --> 06:10:24.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi niya,

asr-005529
06:10:24.340 --> 06:10:26.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: there is always a conference

asr-005530
06:10:26.340 --> 06:10:28.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: where 40 governments

asr-005531
06:10:28.340 --> 06:10:30.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: rise in turn

asr-005532
06:10:30.340 --> 06:10:32.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: to pledge a sovereign cloud,

asr-005533
06:10:32.340 --> 06:10:34.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a sovereign model,

asr-005534
06:10:34.340 --> 06:10:38.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: a national champion of their very own.

asr-005535
06:10:38.340 --> 06:10:39.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Ibig sabihin,

asr-005536
06:10:39.340 --> 06:10:40.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: eh, mga iba't ibang bansa,

asr-005537
06:10:40.340 --> 06:10:43.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: gusto nila magkaroon ng sarili nilang AI.

asr-005538
06:10:43.340 --> 06:10:44.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: No?

asr-005539
06:10:44.340 --> 06:10:47.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: They will applaud one another's independence.

asr-005540
06:10:47.340 --> 06:10:49.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Then they will go home

asr-005541
06:10:49.340 --> 06:10:51.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: and pour billions

asr-005542
06:10:51.340 --> 06:10:53.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: into companies built to do

asr-005543
06:10:53.340 --> 06:10:57.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: precisely what 39 others are doing

asr-005544
06:10:57.340 --> 06:10:59.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: in markets too small

asr-005545
06:10:59.340 --> 06:11:02.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: to sustain even one of them.

asr-005546
06:11:02.340 --> 06:11:07.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Chasing margins that thin asymptotically toward nothing

asr-005547
06:11:07.340 --> 06:11:10.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: the moment the next champion is announced.

asr-005548
06:11:10.340 --> 06:11:13.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: They will have achieved not so-called

asr-005549
06:11:13.340 --> 06:11:15.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: digital sovereignty

asr-005550
06:11:15.340 --> 06:11:19.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: but a kind of synchronized mediocrity

asr-005551
06:11:19.340 --> 06:11:22.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: as planet of sub-scale clones

asr-005552
06:11:22.340 --> 06:11:26.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: each heroically reconstructing last year's breakthrough

asr-005553
06:11:26.340 --> 06:11:30.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: while the breakthrough itself moves on without them.

asr-005554
06:11:30.340 --> 06:11:32.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, pinagtatawanan po ni Helberg

asr-005555
06:11:32.340 --> 06:11:34.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: yung ginagawa ng DOST.

asr-005556
06:11:34.340 --> 06:11:35.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Sabi niya,

asr-005557
06:11:35.340 --> 06:11:36.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: hibang kayo,

asr-005558
06:11:36.340 --> 06:11:37.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: nag-i-invest kayo.

asr-005559
06:11:37.340 --> 06:11:39.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: In this case, ang hinihingi niyo po,

asr-005560
06:11:39.340 --> 06:11:41.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: magkano nga po ulit yung hinihingi niyo?

asr-005561
06:11:41.340 --> 06:11:42.340
Rep. Amben S. Amante: Ah,

asr-005562
06:11:42.340 --> 06:11:43.340
Rep. Amben S. Amante: 300 million.

asr-005563
06:11:43.340 --> 06:11:44.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: 300 million.

asr-005564
06:11:44.340 --> 06:11:45.340
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: This year, 600.

asr-005565
06:11:45.340 --> 06:11:46.340
